    "measurementTechnique": [
      "This reporting format (RF) was developed as part of the DOE-BER-ESS initiative to improve the alignment of organization, terminology, and structure of data files submitted to the ESS-DIVE data archive, in order to increase findability, machine-readability, and re-useability of data produced by ESS-funded research groups. The RF for soil/sediment/water sample chemical concentration data builds on the RFs for sample metadata, file level metadata (FLMD), and csv files developed in parallel.\nIn addition, to ascertain a broad support and acceptance of the RF among the ESS research groups, we received input from members of the community that regularly collect chemical concentration data from the types of samples targeted by this RF:\nLawrence Berkeley National Laboratory Watershed Function SFA\nArgonne National Laboratory Wetland Hydrobiogeochemistry SFA\nPacific Northwest National Laboratory River Corridor Hydrobiogeochemistry SFA\nSLAC National Accelerator Laboratory Floodplain Hydrobiogeochemistry SFA\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory Biogeochemistry at Interfaces SFA\nOak Ridge National Laboratory\nIn addition to providing general information about their current data organization and archiving approaches, several of these community members tested the templates and provided additional feedback on the suitability and ease-of-use for their particular projects and data.\nFinally, discussions with the community members developing other RFs provided guidance on how to best structure the RF, the documentation, and terminology to optimize alignment among the RFs.\nIt should be noted that although several existing vocabularies and ontologies were reviewed as part of the process, none was found to suit the needs of the ESS community and, hence, we decided to only provide guidance on HOW to use/structure terms and WHAT information to include rather than specific recommendations on terminology/vocabulary (except for terms used in upstream RFs \u2013 i.e. flmd, csv_dd, and sample_metadata RFs)."
    ],
